 REACTION MODELING IN FAST NEUTRON RANGE                          2625 1451
 ---------------------------------------                          2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
 The fast region calculations were performed using the EMPIRE     2625 1451
 code, which is a comprehensive package that integrates into a    2625 1451
 single system a number of important physical modules and         2625 1451
 evaluation tools. We have adopted coupled channel (CC)           2625 1451
 calculations in the incident channel and for the direct          2625 1451
 inelastic scattering to collective levels. In addition, we       2625 1451
 have allowed for the Distorted Wave Born Approximation (DWBA)    2625 1451
 to populate presumably collective levels which are not           2625 1451
 included in the ground state band used in the CC calculations    2625 1451
 to adjust neutron emission spectra in the high energy range.     2625 1451
 For the preequilibrium (PE) emission employed the classical      2625 1451
 exciton model (PCROSS module) because of its higher              2625 1451
 flexibility in modeling neutron spectra compared with the        2625 1451
 physically more advanced, but also more rigid quantum            2625 1451
 mechanical models. The same module was also used for the PE      2625 1451
 emission of protons and gammas as well as for PE emission of     2625 1451
 clusters, the latter taking advantage of the Iwamoto-Harada      2625 1451
 model.                                                           2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
 The Hauser-Feshbach formulation of the statistical model was     2625 1451
 employed to follow sequential emission of particles from the     2625 1451
 compound nucleus (CN). The elastic and inelastic angular         2625 1451
 distributions of neutrons emitted from the CN were calculated    2625 1451
 using the Blatt-Biedenharn formalism. The width fluctuation      2625 1451
 factor was accounted for within HRTW formalism applied up to     2625 1451
 12.0 MeV incident neutrons. Compound nucleus and direct cross    2625 1451
 sections were added incoherently.                                2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
 Gilbert-Cameron model for level-density has been adopted due     2625 1451
 to it performance on the 56Fe(n,p) reaction that is extremely    2625 1451
 sensitive to level densities. Level density parameters were      2625 1451
 fitted to reproduce the asymptotic behavior of discrete          2625 1451
 levels, as well as to correctly describe the observed cross      2625 1451
 sections.                                                        2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
 Complete g-ray cascades for every excited nucleus were           2625 1451
 calculated using M1, E1 and E2 electromagnetic transitions.      2625 1451
 g-strength functions for E1 transitions from the RIPL3 MLO1      2625 1451
 formulation by Pluyko.                                           2625 1451
 Occasionally, we resorted to energy-dependent parameter          2625 1451
 scaling or tuning factors, available in the EMPIRE code, to      2625 1451
 account for model deficiencies. These corrections were           2625 1451
 typically on the level of 1-2% or less and can be found in the   2625 1451
 input files. Whenever possible the reaction model parameters     2625 1451
 used in the 54Fe evaluation were kept consistent with those      2625 1451
 used in the 56Fe evaluation.                                     2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
 FAST NEUTRON RANGE                                               2625 1451
 ------------------                                               2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
 MF=3 Neutron cross sections                                      2625 1451
   EMPIRE calculations adjusted to reproduce experimental data    2625 1451
   were adopted unless stated differently below.                  2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
  MT=1 Total                                                      2625 1451
    The cross sections were calculated with the EMPIRE code using 2625 1451
    an optical potential #614 in RIPL-3. The energy-dependent     2625 1451
    scaling was applied below 2 MeV to reproduce elastic Guenther 2625 1451
    data  [7] and to improve agreement with averaged ENDF-VII.1   2625 1451
    between 700 keV and 1.2 MeV.                                  2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
  MT=2 Elastic scattering                                         2625 1451
    Smooth EMPIRE calculations above the resonance region were    2625 1451
    adopted.                                                      2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
 MT=4, 51-91 Inelastic scattering                                 2625 1451
   Results of EMPIRE calculations were adopted.  Limited          2625 1451
   experimental data available indicate the possibility of a      2625 1451
   fluctuating structure similar to the one observed in 56Fe.     2625 1451
   Such a pattern is expected in all even isotopes of iron as the 2625 1451
   nuclear structure of these nuclei is similar. The data,        2625 1451
   however, are not sufficient to unambiguously establish the     2625 1451
   shape of the fluctuating cross sections.                       2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
  MT=5 (n,anything)                                               2625 1451
    Sum of all reactions not given explicitly in another MT       2625 1451
    number as calculated by the EMPIRE code. This MT includes     2625 1451
    majority of the reaction channels - namely all those for which2625 1451
    we do not provide a complete set of exclusive emission        2625 1451
    spectra. The reason for this unusual representation is a      2625 1451
    difficulty to disentangle contributions of different reactions2625 1451
    to the gamma spectrum from the final residue. This becomes an 2625 1451
    issue at higher incident energies when multiple reactions     2625 1451
    contribute to the production of a given residue. Note that    2625 1451
    exclusive gamma emission spectrum is required by the ENDF-6   2625 1451
    format for each reaction that is treated as exclusive. In the 2625 1451
    MT=5 representation, the cross sections can be obtained by    2625 1451
    multiplying cumulative cross section given in MT=5 by the     2625 1451
    relative yields for production of the residual nuclei given in2625 1451
    the subsections of MF/MT=6/5. Particle and gamma emission     2625 1451
    spectra are summed up over the MT=5 reactions into the        2625 1451
    inclusive spectra given in the respective subsections of MF/  2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
 MT=6/5.                                                          2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
  MT=102 Capture                                                  2625 1451
    EMPIRE calculations were adopted.  Between 200 and 500 keV    2625 1451
    they were tuned to agree with Allen data  [8].                2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
  MT=16 (n,2n)                                                    2625 1451
    The 54Fe(n, 2n) channel was fitted simultaneously with the (n,2625 1451
    p) and (n,a) reactions. In this case, since the IRDFF [55, 56]2625 1451
    dosimetry evaluation was available for all three reactions,   2625 1451
    IRDFF was used as fitting guidance instead of actual          2625 1451
    experimental data. Around 15 to 20 MeV the experimental data  2625 1451
    present two conflicting trends. Our evaluation follows the    2625 1451
    lower trend and the data above 20 MeV. Ultimately, the total  2625 1451
    54 Fe(n, 2n) (ground plus meta-stable states) was replaced by 2625 1451
    the IRDFF evaluation. In the energy region close to the       2625 1451
    reaction threshold the new evaluation is significantly lower  2625 1451
    than all other evaluations, which is well supported by the    2625 1451
    results of the new Wallner experiment.                        2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
  MT=17, 22, 28, 107, ...,849                                     2625 1451
    EMPIRE calculations adjusted to reproduce experimental data.  2625 1451
    MTs NOT present! Included in MT=5.                            2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
  MT=103, 600-609, 649 (n,p)                                      2625 1451
    This reaction has been adjusted to reproduce the IRDFF        2625 1451
    evaluation by fitting level-density parameters. In addition,  2625 1451
    the optical model parameters for the residue nucleus 54Mn were2625 1451
    changed globally up to 10%. To obtain a particularly good fit 2625 1451
    around the (n, p) peak, an energy-dependent fit of optical    2625 1451
    potential parameters was introduced between 4.5 and 9.5 MeV.  2625 1451
    Ultimately, MT=103 was below 20 MeV was replaced by the IRDFF 2625 1451
    cross sections.                                               2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
  MT=111, (n,2p)                                                  2625 1451
    EMPIRE calculations adjusted to reproduce experimental data.  2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
  MT=800-818 (n,a_discrete)                                       2625 1451
    Alpha emission (from both discrete levels and continuum) from 2625 1451
    the compound nucleus was tuned between 5 and 20 MeV in order  2625 1451
    to closely reproduce the (n, a) cross section from IRDFF.     2625 1451
    Additionally, the optical model parameters the 54Fe(n,a)      2625 1451
    residue, 51Cr, were changed up to 6% and the alpha emission   2625 1451
    from the compound nucleus was tuned between 5 and 21 MeV,     2625 1451
    leading to an excellent agreement with IRDFF.                 2625 1451
    NOTE: Full (n,a) reaction is NOT given in the file (i.e., no  2625 1451
    MT=107) as explained in the original paper. MT=849            2625 1451
    (n,a_continuum) is added to MT=5.                             2625 1451
