 CROSS SECTION COVARIANCES                                        2625 1451
 -------------------------                                        2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
 MF=33                                                            2625 1451
   Covariances were determined using Kalman filter-inspired       2625 1451
   Bayesian update procedure. This methodology combines           2625 1451
   experimental uncertainties with the model constraints imposed  2625 1451
   through the sensitivity profiles provided by the EMPIRE code.  2625 1451
   Using KALMAN, the model parameters were sequentially adjusted  2625 1451
   to each considered experiment. Cross section covariances are   2625 1451
   obtained by propagating covariances of the model parameters.   2625 1451
   The covariances were computed for the major reaction channels  2625 1451
   represented in the evaluations: total, elastic, inelastic,     2625 1451
   capture, (n, 2n), and (n, p). Inelastic scattering to          2625 1451
   individual discrete levels (MT=51,...,90) and to the continuum 2625 1451
   (MT=91) were combined together into MT=4. In addition,         2625 1451
   covariances for the sum of all the remaining channels (MT=5)   2625 1451
   are provided. Experimental uncertainties reported in EXFOR, if 2625 1451
   available, were used to determine the long-range correlations  2625 1451
   in the experimental covariance matrices. If such information   2625 1451
   was not available 45% correlation between different energy     2625 1451
   points for the same reaction was assumed. The experimental     2625 1451
   datasets showing pronounced fluctuation structure were         2625 1451
   smoothed before being used.                                    2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
   The EMPIRE/KALMAN genrated covariances were extended over the  2625 1451
   resonance region. Since actual uncertainties of the thermal    2625 1451
   constants and resonance paprameters were not considered these  2625 1451
   covariances are very conservative and should be considered as  2625 1451
   an upper limit of uncertainties.                               2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
   In the case of (n,2n) and (n,p) reaction where IRDFF cross     2625 1451
   sections were used in the evaluation procedure in place of the 2625 1451
   experimental datasets it was desirable to retain, as far as    2625 1451
   possible, also IRDFF covariances. We preserved KALMAN created  2625 1451
   covariances but during the procedure, we adjusted weights of   2625 1451
   the IRDFF cross sections to reproduce, as closely as possible, 2625 1451
   the original IRDFF uncertainties.                              2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
 EMPIRE CODE PARAMETRIZATION                                      2625 1451
 ---------------------------                                      2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
 Nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-3.2.3 Malta                   2625 1451
 (SVN rev. 4977; source rev. 4977)                                2625 1451
 by M.W.Herman et al [11,12].                                     2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
 EMPIRE dimensions (dimension.h):                                 2625 1451
 NDNUC= 160 NDEXCLUS= 50 NDEX= 241 NDLW= 100                      2625 1451
 LEVCC= 40 NDLV= 40 NDBR= 40 NDMSCS= 4                            2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
 The following EMPIRE-code modules and features were used in      2625 1451
 the current evaluation:                                          2625 1451
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 2625 1451
   coupled-channels code ECIS06 by J. Raynal                      2625 1451
 - Soft-rotator deformed Optical Model including                  2625 1451
   coupled-channels code OPTMAN by E.Soukhovitskii                2625 1451
   and coworkers                                                  2625 1451
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    2625 1451
   width fluctuation correction, and the                          2625 1451
   optical model for fission with partial damping                 2625 1451
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      2625 1451
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 2625 1451
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                2625 1451
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   2625 1451
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                2625 1451
   discrete transitions                                           2625 1451
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL library [RIPL]                2625 1451
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                2625 1451
   level density, discrete levels,                                2625 1451
   and gamma strength functions based on the RIPL                 2625 1451
   library [13]                                                   2625 1451
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              2625 1451
   EXFOR library                                                  2625 1451
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A.Trkov)                     2625 1451
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 2625 1451
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                2625 1451
   PrePro codes by D. Cullen                                      2625 1451
 - ENDF checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                   2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
                      EMPIRE options                              2625 1451
                      --------------                              2625 1451
 Following options and deviations from the default values of      2625 1451
 the parameters were employed in the EMPIRE calculations:         2625 1451
                                                                  2625 1451
 - CC calculations using soft-rotor omp for the incident channel. 2625 1451
 - CN decay and Direct cross sections added incoherently.         2625 1451
 - Traditional Hauser-Feschbach Tlj_{CC}(E)=Tlj_{GS}(E-Egs).      2625 1451
 - HRTW width fluctuation correction calculated  up to 12.10 MeV. 2625 1451
 - Tlj coupling for the top CN bin  up to incident  9.90 MeV.     2625 1451
 - CN anisotropy calculated using Blatt-Biedenharn coefficients.  2625 1451
 - Coupled Channels Method used for Tl calcul. in outgoing ch.    2625 1451
 - Discrete levels were taken from the RIPL-3+                    2625 1451
    library based on the 2015 version of ENSDF.                   2625 1451
 - Gamma-transition multipolarity set to 2.                       2625 1451
 - GDR parameters taken from RIPL/Exp.data+Plujko systematics.    2625 1451
 - E1 strength function set to RIPL MLO1                          2625 1451
 - Gilbert-Cameron (EMPIRE 2.18) level densities.                 2625 1451
 - Preequilibrium mechanism treated in terms of the exciton model 2625 1451
    with the Iwamoto-Harada model for emission of clusters, and   2625 1451
    Kalbach systematics angular distributions (see RIPL-1)        2625 1451
